From e34dc7e426af0a96f7add59aa52a9108e52a803b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Cast: implement cast framework session lifecycle

Apps bundling play-services-cast-framework load the cast framework
dynamite module from microG and drive sessions through it. Several parts
of that path were missing, so no session could ever be started:

- The module never registered its media router callback with the
  client's MediaRouter, so route selections never reached it.
- Current client libraries register their CastSession provider under
  categories like CATEGORY_CAST/<APPID>///ALLOW_IPV6. The module
  recomputed CATEGORY_CAST/<APPID>, so the provider lookup failed.
- ISession notify* calls, startSession, endCurrentSession and the cast
  state were not implemented.

Implement the session state machine (start, resume, suspend, end),
launch or join the receiver application, report the cast state from
route availability, track app visibility for discovery, recover the
last session, and implement the reconnection service and bitmap
fetching used for media notifications.

Align the binder interfaces with the transaction codes current client
libraries use (dynamite module and media router callback versions,
session start type, route info updates, IMediaRouter additions,
ConnectionResult in ICastSession.onConnectionFailed) and add a dynamite
module descriptor for the cast framework module instead of the
hardcoded version in DynamiteLoaderImpl.
